WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.868
- So pretty.
- What's pretty, Lena?

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:03.868
- Miu.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.960
- Let's make it to Disneyland.
- Fine by me. Just no roller coasters.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:12.520
We should ride one… but we'll go together.
Just close your eyes.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:21.800 line:0
<i>ขิง (khing): ginger; Thai slang for "to show off"</i>

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.120
- Do you eat "khing"?
- No?

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.280
- But I like to "khing."
- Ginger?

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.880
- You like to "khing," as a verb.
- Brag, yeah.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:26.924
- Hello!
- Hello!

00:00:26.924 --> 00:00:29.040
- Hello, today…
- Hello, hi!

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.920
Today's our day off.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.137
We're out to do something fun…

00:00:34.137 --> 00:00:37.840
and this seems like a place
Miu would never come to.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.360
I love it here.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.640
- She didn't say that earlier.
- Really?

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:43.640
- Mm.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:46.720
You sure you heard that right?
She didn't say that earlier.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.680 line:0
<i>Miu really loves it here</i>

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.840
She's right. I would never come here.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.849
- First, it makes me dizzy.

00:00:54.849 --> 00:00:59.280
- It's fun, though.
You get the experience without doing much.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:02.080
This place doesn't take much effort.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.594
- No, you don't. It's…

00:01:03.594 --> 00:01:06.853
- Lena loves it.
It's more for an adrenaline rush.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.800 line:0
<i>Right up Lena's alley</i>

00:01:06.853 --> 00:01:09.200
- No need to run around or anything.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.320
Take a look.
At least this one looks okay.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.400
It's in 3D or 4D,
but they only have horror.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:16.980 line:0
<i>Lena loves it</i>

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.120
I love that.
I've been doing this since I was a kid.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.769
It was 100 baht for a show
under 10 minutes, though.

00:01:22.769 --> 00:01:25.720
Pretty expensive for a kid,
but I loved it.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.520
- Okay.
- Let's try it. To the mirror room then.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.480
- Doubt they have one.
- Do they?

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.480
- They do.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:34.400
- Ever walked into a mirror? Bam!
- Never.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:39.695
- Let's see if she bumps her head today.
- No way.

00:01:39.695 --> 00:01:42.240
- Come on, let's go bump some heads.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.400
- Put it on.
- I got this.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.920
- Give me your leg.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.359
- You already did yours?
- Yeah.

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:51.080
- Now the other one.
- Oh?

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:54.280
I see. Want to take care of her, huh?

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.744
- Not really.
- Nope.

00:01:56.744 --> 00:01:58.560
- She wanted to.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:04.520
Open sesame! Open sesame.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.920
No, it's the dizzy room!

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.120
We've done this before.
This one's really dizzying.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.560
- Oh?
- It started? I love this.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.560 line:0
<i>The room Lena looked forward to</i>

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.760
Even the sound is thrilling.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.340 line:0
<i>Not going in</i>

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.781
- Don't ever close the curtain.
- Why?

00:02:39.781 --> 00:02:41.680
- Close it and I'm definitely dead…

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.280 line:0
<i>Miu's too scared to watch</i>

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.480
I can't. I can't breathe.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:49.320
Come on, the ghost's about to pop out.
It's coming. There's a ball.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:53.120
- That's a jump scare for sure.
- Yeah, it's going to pop out.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:53.120 line:0
<i>Too scared</i>

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.030
- Ready to run?
- Where to?

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:58.440
- I'm ready.
- Come on!

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:01.240
- Oh? Huh?
- That was just a teaser.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.960
Is this it? Huh… there's more?

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.960
- There! Found it.
- I see the edge.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:19.960
- It's here.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.840
I don't really trust you.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.320
Look, a ball pit!

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.900 line:0
<i>Ball pit</i>

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.440
Oh… No, we're…

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.800
One… Two…

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:43.760
- We screamed like kids!
- Yeah. I was so excited sliding down.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:47.320
Haven't done this in ages. Take this!

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:54.480
Wow.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.030
- This is cute.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:04.360
- So pretty.
Like we're out in space. Pretty.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.898
- What's pretty, Lena?
- Miu.

00:04:06.898 --> 00:04:08.000
- Aww.
- See?

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:13.320
- Because she only shows her back.
- That's so mean!

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:18.680
Was that a roast? Huh? But seriously,
Lena looked really pretty in the photos.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:21.630
- Because?
- Because she faced the camera.

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:22.630
- Aww!

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:25.120
Wipe the lens first.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:35.680
We're here. I used to do this as a kid.
This is it. Wow, this takes me back.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:38.480
Next, Disneyland.
Lena's riding roller coasters.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:40.060 line:0
<i>Scared to death</i>

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.668
- Please don't.
- What rides won't you do?

00:04:41.668 --> 00:04:43.000
- Roller coasters.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:46.440
Yeah, this one too. The up-and-down one…
still gives me chills.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:51.880
I tried one in Canada, maybe the tallest.
I cried when I got off.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.760 line:0
<i>Traumatized</i>

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.760
I couldn't even scream.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.355
- Look, Godzilla!
- She's sleepy?!

00:05:02.355 --> 00:05:03.840
- She's yawning!

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:26.320
- I want something scary.
Is the horror one next?

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:27.320
- Whee!

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:30.240
- What?
- A special horror round. Let's stay.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:34.320
Hey, that was fun!
I'm only here for horror.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:34.320 line:0
<i>Lena totally loves it</i>

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.120
- We're showing Nightmare next.
- Huh? Nightmare?

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:43.200
Are you scared of zombies?
There's roaches too!

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.200
That startled me.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:18.240
Here it comes. This is a horror ride!
Why's it a roller coaster now? Here we go.

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:33.960
- No!
- Don't close your eyes! You have to look!

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:49.160
Oh, my god… Oh…

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:55.200
Lena's dying inside.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.280
This isn't helping!

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.080
She's scared.

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:25.920
It wasn't that scary.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:31.800
Deep down, we knew we were safe,
if you know what I mean.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:37.160
I've been avoiding roller coasters.
But in the end…

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.000 line:0
<i>Had to ride one eventually</i>

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:41.800
It was somewhat scary,
but the horror part was satisfying.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:46.720
- Let's make it to Disneyland.
- Fine by me. Just no roller coasters.

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:46.720 line:0
<i>Let's go to Disneyland</i>

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:51.320
We should ride one… but we'll go together.
Just close your eyes.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.320 line:0
<i>Trust me, okay?</i>

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.720
- You'll warm up to it.
- That'd ruin my day.

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:59.160
My dad took me on every ride. I'd cry,
but he still took me. Now I love it.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:03.480
- It'll grow on you.
- So you had to beat the fear first?

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:06.480
Then you'll be like,
"Whoo! I love this!"

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:08.920 line:0
<i>I've seen too much</i>

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:08.920
I've seen too much Final Destination.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:10.736
- Never saw them. I can't watch.

00:08:10.736 --> 00:08:14.480
- I watched them too many times…
now I'm paranoid it'll happen to me.

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:17.840
- We're eating next, right?
- She only cares about food.

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:21.154
Bring your date here for an experience…

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:21.340 line:0
<i>A date?</i>

00:08:21.154 --> 00:08:24.720
or hang out with friends
at 3D attractions.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:27.560
- Cave Fantasy is totally for you!
- Yes.

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:34.960
Now we're going to get lunch.
We're heading to Siam Square.

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:34.960 line:0
<i>Let's get lunch</i>

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:39.063
- Right, we rarely get to go out like this.
- Yeah.

00:08:39.063 --> 00:08:40.640
- So we'll go today.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:43.320
- There's lots to see.
- Yes.

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:46.708
- Ooh! Over there… our ad!
- It's LenaMiu!

00:08:46.708 --> 00:08:48.080
- Film it, quick!

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:50.680
No, I missed it!

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:53.120 line:0
<i>Saw the ad they did</i>

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:56.809
- I thought it was BTS's Jungkook,
so I didn't pay attention…

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:56.680 line:0
<i>Didn't think it was themselves</i>

00:08:56.809 --> 00:08:58.880
- but my face was on it!
- LenaMiu!

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:01.600
- I got some good pics. See?
- Yes, here.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.692
- And…
- Hey, that's nice.

00:09:03.692 --> 00:09:07.640
- Pretty good, yeah?
That's my go-to profile angle.

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:22.840
Let's see what Ms. Lalina will order.

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:34.200
This is our go-to choice, miso soup!

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:44.000
We might share the same taste,
but not in Japanese food. Strange, right?

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:49.920
Back then, I didn't eat raw fish.
Only started less than five years ago.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:51.601
- But you don't eat it?
- No.

00:09:51.601 --> 00:09:52.760
- Not at all?
- Nope.

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:55.492
Probably because I don't like seafood.

00:09:55.492 --> 00:09:59.120
And raw fish… the texture…
plus seafood has a smell.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.840
- Not really my thing.
- It's not her thing.

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:06.880
- But if it's cooked, like salmon?
- Yeah, that's fine.

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:13.000
Oh, my order's here. I'll show you.
Look, it's so pretty.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:14.947
- What did you get? Oh, salmon.

00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:18.200
- Salmon. Mine's shrimp with
yuzu yogurt or something.

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:19.320
Yogurt?

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:28.640
- It's good. Very good.
- Good?

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:33.280
Ikura avocado. Bad angle. I love ikura.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:36.223
- This is tamagoyaki.
- I don't eat rolled omelet.

00:10:36.223 --> 00:10:37.884
- Because it's sweet?
- Yeah.

00:10:37.884 --> 00:10:38.884
- But I love it.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.400
The seaweed's crispy.

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:55.600 line:0
<i>ขิง (khing): ginger; Thai slang for "to show off"</i>

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:47.080
- Want some "khing"?
- No?

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:49.280
- But I like to "khing."
- Ginger?

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:52.098
- Are you trying to make a pun?

00:10:52.098 --> 00:10:55.600
- Yep. Still gonna "khing"
about lunch with you, though.

00:10:55.680 --> 00:11:00.320
- Ooh, let me get this.
- We just had it yesterday.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:06.360
- It's too big. Wanna share?
- I'm good.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:16.120
- That was superb.
Let's hit the next spot.

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:19.156
- We're on a food tour.
After Japanese, next is…

00:11:19.156 --> 00:11:20.800
- Thai.
- Yeah, Thai food.

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:23.741
- Do you guys go out often?

00:11:23.741 --> 00:11:27.600
- Not really. We're usually busy.
This is a rare moment…

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:29.157
- Not even in school.

00:11:29.157 --> 00:11:33.800
- In school? Back then… I came here often,
but mostly to the mall.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:39.400
I just went home after class.
During the pandemic, I didn't go out much.

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:44.160
My school was in Ratchadamri…
just one Skytrain stop from here.

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:46.800
I see. Oh, we're here! Kate Teaw.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:52.360 line:0
<i>Kate Teaw</i>

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:56.280
- They have small portions. Let's get that.
- Get ten!

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:56.540 line:0
<i>Ten!!</i>

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:57.280
- Yeah.

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:00.369
- Can't do ten today,
but I've had ten before. Love them.

00:12:00.369 --> 00:12:02.320
- What's your record?
- Four… three.

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.520
Thin noodles, wide noodles, vermicelli.

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:10.760
This is… vermicelli boat noodles
with Thai wagyu beef, not spicy.

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:15.473
- Mine? Wide noodles.
- Why "wide noodles"?

00:12:15.473 --> 00:12:17.520
- I keep it simple.

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:18.600
Can I post this?

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:29.160
- The pork's a bit sweet.
- Sweet?

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:32.794
- Your pork's really good.
- It's good, right?

00:12:32.794 --> 00:12:34.880
- The noodles and soup too.

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:36.980 line:0
<i>Got a stain on her shirt</i>

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:39.955
- Don't worry. I've got this.
- I knew you'd spill.

00:12:39.955 --> 00:12:41.160
- Done, I wiped it.

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:49.040
- I brought this for you.
- It's fine. It's not obvious.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.200
- You take good care of her.
- Of course.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:52.200
- Two orders?

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:57.720
- I've seen her spill a lot. I know my cue.
- Really?

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:03.091
- Ugh, cracklings make me sigh.
Want some? It's good.

00:13:03.091 --> 00:13:05.000
- No, I prefer pork rinds.

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:08.400
- What are they bringing us?
- Morning glory noodles.

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:17.280 line:0
<i>Taking turns taking care of each other</i>

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:18.227
- If I spot a loose strand of hair…
- I'll move it.

00:13:18.227 --> 00:13:20.800
- Yeah, me too. It's annoying, right?

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:25.880
- So you mostly eat on your day off?
- Yeah, but I liked what we did today.

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:27.460 line:0
<i>I like it</i>

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:29.685
- It's relaxing.
- No, you just like eating.

00:13:29.685 --> 00:13:30.685
- Oh…

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:38.840
It's their must-try new dish.
It's good for… people who prefer low carb.

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:44.640
You get fiber from veggie noodles too.
They cut morning glory into thin strips.

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:54.080
I like it. Love it. I love morning glory.
It's perfect for boat noodles.

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:56.000
- Yeah.
- I love it like that.

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:06.320
Oh, it comes with… I see.

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:10.200
Look, you can also save it for later.

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:14.818
- That fits Lena. She loves nibbling…
- takes her time.

00:14:14.818 --> 00:14:16.200
- Yeah, I eat slowly.

00:14:16.280 --> 00:14:17.360
It's good.

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:29.280
It's like what's sold in…
those old-school toast shops.

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:34.320
I can taste the rainbow.
So good. Truly a one-stop meal.

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:49.617
- I'm satisfied now.
- I'm spent.

00:14:49.617 --> 00:14:53.600
- This is super good! Let's take some home.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:59.291
- We're ending this vlog exhausted.
- We're not tired, just…

00:14:59.291 --> 00:15:00.920
- so full.
- Food coma.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.926
Yeah, food coma. I can't anymore.

00:15:03.926 --> 00:15:08.360
Our bodies are digesting food now,
so we're tired.

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:10.560
- Let's go home and sleep.
- For real.

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:11.560
- Yeah.

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:15.720
- Bye, everyone!
- Bye! Hope you enjoyed this vlog.

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:22.680
For noodles or great old-school toast,
come check out Kate Teaw.

00:15:22.760 --> 00:15:28.520
- And if you're on a diet… there's…
- Morning glory noodles.

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:30.371
Yeah, morning glory noodles.

00:15:30.371 --> 00:15:34.040
Boat noodles with morning glory…
that's a fiber-rich dish.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:37.040
- We're going now.
- Bye-bye!

